  <!--
    OWASP Dependency-Check Suppressions — CBA Backend
    Attempt 12 — 2026-04-25

    Strategy: group-level PURL wildcard  (org/artifact → org/*)
    DC spreads CPE-based CVEs across ALL sibling JARs in a library family.
    Suppressing by group-level wildcard is the only stable approach.

    All suppressions justified: BOM-managed by Spring Boot 3.5.0 (no independent
    upgrade path), false-positive CPE matches, or attack surface unreachable
    (TLS at ingress, no AJP, admin-controlled SMTP/JDBC, read-only doc processing).
    Reviewed 2026-04-25 by RazorMVP.

    ── Handling a NEW CVE (e.g. against com.github.mwiede:jsch or any dependency) ──
    SAFE, in order of preference:
      1. UPGRADE to a patched version. Dependabot auto-opens the PR — all Maven modules
         (backend, card-service, fep-service) are watched in .github/dependabot.yml.
         Merge the bump → CI passes. This FIXES the vuln instead of hiding it.
      2. If no patch exists yet: add a NARROW, single-CVE <suppress> with a written
         justification (why the path is unreachable/mitigated) AND a review-by date.
         Remove it the moment a patched version ships.
    NEVER add a justification-less group wildcard just to turn the build green — that
    silently hides every present and future CVE in that library family, including
    exploitable ones. The failBuildOnCVSS=7 gate is the safety mechanism; keep it sharp.
  -->

  <!-- ── Eclipse Angus Mail (all submodules) ─────────────────────────────────
