  <!-- Data-binding DoS via user-supplied property paths.
       ⚠️ NOT claimed unreachable — this is a RISK-ACCEPTED entry. -->
  <suppress until="2026-12-22Z">
    <notes>No fixed release exists (affects every Spring 5.2–7.0 line). Risk accepted,
      NOT unreachable: the classic vector is absent — no @ModelAttribute, no
      WebDataBinder/@InitBinder, and all 188 request payloads bind as JSON through
      Jackson rather than Spring property paths — but Spring Data's Pageable/Sort
      resolution does accept user-supplied property names, so a DoS attempt cannot be
      fully excluded. Mitigations: authenticated endpoints only, plus per-tier rate
      limiting (RateLimitFilter). Upgrade the moment a fixed Spring release ships.</notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework/.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-59282</cve>
  </suppress>

